# Kestrel Yard: a freight yard in the built-up end of a works town.
#
# Radius 14 — 29 hexes and 50 m across — against the waystation's 24, asked for on purpose: entry
# 007 reasoned the size from the ranges, and a town blocks the ranges. Every wall here is a
# building face, the streets are two and three hexes wide, and the longest clear line on the map
# is the main street.
#
# A block is the rectangle between two hex centres (content/README.md). On a flat-topped grid a
# column is straight and a row is a zigzag, so a building's north and south faces step, and two
# blocks that are meant to meet have to share the row of their top or bottom corner.

map Kestrel

# The canal, which is the waystation's stream by another name: no bottom to stand on.
ground deep noise 2 impassable

# ---- ground ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

fill disc 0,0 r 14 floor

# The cut: a canal channel down the west side, too deep and too steep-sided to get out of, with a
# towpath along the east bank and a strip of scrub on the far side that belongs to nobody.
fill line -11,-3 to -11,14 deep
fill line -10,-4 to -10,14 deep
fill hexes -14,0 -14,1 -14,2 -14,3 -14,4 -14,5 -14,6 -14,7 -14,8 -14,9 -14,10 -14,11 -14,12 -14,13 -14,14 grass
fill line -13,-1 to -13,14 grass
fill line -12,-2 to -12,14 grass
fill line -9,-5 to -9,14 mud

# ---- the compound -------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The yard and the shed behind one perimeter wall, with the gate on the main street. The yard is
# hardcore — gravel — because lorries turn on it, which makes it the loudest ground on the map.
fill block -8,0 to 5,7 floor
fill block -8,-4 to 5,-1 gravel
enclose solid block -8,0 to 5,7
breach 0,-4 s sw se
breach 1,-4 s

# A gap in the west wall onto the towpath, where a lorry backed into it and nobody has paid to
# put it right. The first dozen matches fought here had the shed's side door opening into an
# alley inside the wall — a door you could only reach by walking through the gate first, which is
# no way in at all — and every squad in all twelve used the gate.
breach -8,9 sw

# The freight shed. Its roof is glazed sheeting that will not take a man's weight, so there is no
# storey above it to stand on. The loading floor is the east end, where the roller door opens onto
# the yard; the west end is racking. One small door on the west, into the alley inside the wall.
enclose solid block -7,13 to 4,0
breach 2,1 s sw se
breach 3,1 s
breach -7,9 sw

# Racking down the west half of the shed, head-high and full: somewhere to be inside and not be
# seen from the door.
wall high line -5,6 to -5,11 ne
wall high line -3,5 to -3,10 ne
# Pallets on the loading floor itself, knee-high.
wall low hexes 0,7 1,6 2,6 n
wall low hexes 3,3 3,4 sw

# The boiler house behind the shed, outside the wall, and the duct from it that runs under the
# shed's back wall. Nobody on the shift has thought about the duct in years.
enclose solid block -5,13 to -2,13
breach -5,14 sw
link crawl -5,13 -5,12

# ---- the office ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Two storeys across the east lane from the compound wall, and a flat roof. The upper floor's
# west windows look over the wall into the yard and, past the shed's front, into the shed. Stairs
# inside; a fire escape on the east face goes up past the upper floor to the roof, and does not
# stop at a window on the way.
fill hex 12,-4 layer 1 h 3
enclose railing hex 12,-4 layer 1
ladder 12,-4@0 12,-4@1
ladder 12,-4@1 11,-4@2

enclose solid block 7,-6 to 11,-1
breach 7,-3 nw
breach 11,-5 ne
fill block 7,-6 to 11,-1 layer 1 h 3
enclose solid block 7,-6 to 11,-1 layer 1
breach 7,-5@1 nw sw
breach 7,-4@1 nw sw
breach 7,-3@1 nw sw
breach 7,-2@1 nw sw
wall low hexes 7,-5 7,-4 7,-3 7,-2 nw sw layer 1
stairs 10,-3@0 10,-2@1
fill block 7,-6 to 11,-1 layer 2 h 6
enclose railing block 7,-6 to 11,-1 layer 2

# ---- the rest of the street ---------------------------------------------------------------

# The weighbridge hut at the east end of the main street, which is what stops the gate seeing
# round the corner into the east lane.
enclose solid block 7,-9 to 10,-8

# A warehouse north of the office, locked and dark.
enclose solid block 7,3 to 10,3

# The terrace across the main street from the gate: where the shift lives, doors shut.
enclose solid block -6,-8 to -1,-8
enclose solid block 2,-12 to 7,-12

# ---- the way off --------------------------------------------------------------------------

# A footbridge over the cut at the north-west, three metres up, with steps from the towpath. It
# carries on over the embankment beyond the edge of the map, which is where the squad leaves.
fill line -10,13 to -12,14 layer 1 h 3
enclose railing line -10,13 to -12,14 layer 1
breach -10,13@1 se
stairs -9,12@0 -10,13@1
